				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/spikebrennan" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(908688); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=908688&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609905503" alt="spikebrennan" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=908688)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/spikebrennan" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(908688); return false;" >spikebrennan</a></span> <span class="odate time_1327939323 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">30 Jan 2012 16:02</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1361442">
									

<p>The concept is good, but the writing really doesn't do it for me.<br />
Numerous examples:</p>
<p>//&quot;&#8230;pair of of flood lamps used in photography&#8230;&quot; =&gt; &quot;pair of flood lamps of a type typically used in photography&quot;. These lamps - the ones being contained - are not being used in photography, so don't say that they are.</p>
<p><em>&quot;&#8230;however each lamp will display the shadow of an unidentified young woman&#8230;&quot;</em> But this is inconsistent with the content of the observation log, which reveals that additional humanoid shadows will appear. Also, a lamp doesn't &quot;display shadows&quot; in any meaningful sense. Perhaps &quot;&#8230;however each lamp will cause shadows not corresponding to physical objects in the room to appear on the screen&quot; would be better.</p>
<p><em>&quot;&#8230; Whether or not this shadow corresponds to anyone living or dead has yet to be determined, although the shadow appears to re-enact a specific series of events leading up to the woman's death.&quot;</em> Not necessary, and kind of takes some of the punch out of the narrative arc of the observation log. I'd recommend cutting.</p>
<p><em>&quot;SCP-205 will display a still image of one woman in a provocative pose.&quot;</em> SCP-205 is the pair of lamps, so it isn't displaying an image. &quot;The screen in the containment chamber will show a shadow resembling&#8230;&quot; may be better. Also, &quot;provocative pose&quot; is not the best phrase: it could mean anything from a sexually suggestive pose to a rude gesture.</p>
<p><em>&quot;&#8230;the individual displayed appears to be distinct and consistent through all cycles&quot;.</em> I don't know what you're trying to say here.</p>
<p><em>&quot;&#8230;any movement of the atmosphere&#8230;&quot;</em>. &quot;Atmosphere&quot; is the wrong word here; &quot;air&quot; would be clearer.</p>
<p>And so on. I'd urge a top-to-bottom re-write. The clinical tone may also be improved by presenting the observation log in tabular form with time-stamps.</p>
<p>I acknowledge that this sound a bit harsh and out-of-place, given that this is already one of the highest-ranked articles on the site, but there you have it.</p>

